From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: Export retained wide-aspect UHD VIC mappings

Reconcile the existing Linux aaf0b7b36db2 source with the packaged
0079/0080 predecessor. CTA VIC 106 and 107 use the same existing VENC
recipes as UHD50 and UHD60; no new pixel-clock limit or invented VIC.
Physical receiver acceptance is separate from this source declaration.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_venc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_venc.c
@@ -842,6 +842,8 @@
 	{ 95, &meson_hdmi_encp_mode_2160p30 },
 	{ 96, &meson_hdmi_encp_mode_2160p25 },
 	{ 97, &meson_hdmi_encp_mode_2160p30 },
+	{ 106, &meson_hdmi_encp_mode_2160p25 },
+	{ 107, &meson_hdmi_encp_mode_2160p30 },
 	{ 0, NULL}, /* sentinel */
 };
 
